    "notes": "## Decisions\n\n- The Fernhollow duplicate-jobs incident is closed after two days with zero new duplicates since the fix shipped on Tuesday.\n- The read-only offline job list will ship in next week's release, not in today's release cut.\n- The flaky webhook retry integration test is quarantined so it does not gate merges or the release cut.\n- The release cut happens today (Thursday 8 October) at four o'clock; anything that needs to be in must be merged by three thirty.\n- The Outlook time-zone ticket is taken offline to a separate call between Maya and Tom right after standup.\n\n## Key facts\n\n- **When did the Fernhollow dedupe fix go out?** On Tuesday (6 October 2026); there have been zero new duplicates in the two days since.\n- **What is Diego blocked on?** A last modified at field on each job in the jobs list endpoint, which Maya owns, so the mobile app knows when its cached offline copy is stale.\n- **How often has the flaky CI test been failing?** About one in eight runs this week, always on the timeout assertion of the webhook retry integration test.\n- **What does Priya think causes the flaky test?** The test sleeps for a fixed two seconds before checking the retry fired, and CI runners are slower some days; she wants to confirm before saying for sure.\n- **When is the release cut and what is the merge deadline?** Thursday 8 October at four o'clock; merge anything that needs to be in by three thirty.\n- **How many items are on Kestrel Audit's evidence request list?** About sixty; Priya has mapped roughly two thirds to evidence Deino already collects.\n- **How many support tickets were closed yesterday?** Fourteen, nine of which were Fernhollow cleanup confirmations.\n- **What is the new Outlook ticket about?** One technician at a smaller plumbing account sees his jobs an hour off in Outlook; he is in a different time zone from his dispatcher.\n",
    "myNotes": null,
    "actionItems": [
      {
        "title": "Add a last modified at field to each job in the jobs list endpoint for Diego's offline cache",
