    "transcript": [
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 696,
        "end": 6531,
        "text": "Morning, everyone. Let's keep it quick today, I've got a hard stop at quarter to."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 6842,
        "end": 9302,
        "text": "Maya, do you want to kick us off?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 9764,
        "end": 16799,
        "text": "Sure. So yesterday I mostly watched the Fernhollow dashboards after the dedupe fix went out on Tuesday."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 17033,
        "end": 25508,
        "text": "Zero new duplicates in two days, and Owen confirmed the same on his side this morning. So I'm calling the incident closed."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 26201,
        "end": 29001,
        "text": "Nice. That's a big one. Thank you."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 29630,
        "end": 41225,
        "text": "Today I'm back on Calendar Sync v2, writing the subscription renewal part of the design doc. No blockers. And, uh, first morning off the pager, which is lovely."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 41595,
        "end": 44425,
        "text": "Well earned. Okay, Diego, you're up."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 45056,
        "end": 52926,
        "text": "Yeah. Yesterday I got the read-only offline job list caching working on Android. Today I'm starting the iOS side."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 53246,
        "end": 63916,
        "text": "I am kind of blocked, though. I need a last modified at field on each job in the jobs list endpoint, so the app knows when its cached copy is stale."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 64070,
        "end": 73765,
        "text": "Right now I'm diffing the whole payload, which works, but it's slow and it's going to be terrible on a bad connection out in somebody's basement."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 74351,
        "end": 81116,
        "text": "Oh, that one's on me, sorry. I said I'd add it last week and then the incident ate the week."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 81469,
        "end": 86789,
        "text": "It's a small change. I can have it on the endpoint by end of day tomorrow."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 87440,
        "end": 91105,
        "text": "Tomorrow works. I'll stub it on my side until then."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 91485,
        "end": 102970,
        "text": "For context, the Android cache keeps the next fourteen days of jobs for the technician, so it's usually under two hundred jobs. It loads in about a second from cold."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 103383,
        "end": 110213,
        "text": "On iOS I'm reusing the same cache schema, so hopefully it's two or three days of work, not a week."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 110742,
        "end": 115087,
        "text": "Two or three days is fine. Nothing's waiting on it this week."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 115362,
        "end": 118697,
        "text": "Does that mean the offline list misses today's cut?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 119236,
        "end": 129451,
        "text": "Yeah. Honestly it was never really going to make this one. I'd rather it goes out in next week's release with the real field than hack around it."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 129824,
        "end": 135574,
        "text": "Okay, agreed. Offline list goes in next week's release, not this one. Priya?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 136156,
        "end": 148476,
        "text": "Yesterday was mostly SOC 2 prep. Kestrel Audit sent over their evidence request list, it's about sixty items, and I've mapped maybe two thirds of them to things we already collect."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 148684,
        "end": 158594,
        "text": "Kestrel wants the observation window to start cleanly on the first of November, so everything on that list needs an owner by the end of next week."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 158956,
        "end": 167496,
        "text": "I'll send each of you the handful of items that are yours on Monday. Most of it is screenshots of settings, nothing scary."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 168019,
        "end": 170849,
        "text": "Is anything on there going to surprise us?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 171472,
        "end": 181052,
        "text": "Access reviews for the production database, probably. We've never done a formal one. I'll draft a process, but that's a next-week problem."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 181458,
        "end": 192238,
        "text": "The other thing is the flaky test. The webhook retry integration test has failed something like one in eight runs this week, always on the timeout assertion."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 192585,
        "end": 200300,
        "text": "I'm quarantining it this morning so it stops blocking merges, and I'll file a ticket with the logs I've got so far."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 200744,
        "end": 203199,
        "text": "Is it a real bug or just the test?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 204063,
        "end": 217703,
        "text": "I think it's the test. It sleeps for a fixed two seconds and then checks the retry fired, and the CI runners are just slower some days. But I want to look properly before I say that for sure."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 218586,
        "end": 227186,
        "text": "It does touch the retry queue I'm about to rewrite for v2, so I'm happy to pair on it next week if it turns out to be real."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 227855,
        "end": 230840,
        "text": "Maybe. Let's see what the logs say first."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 231259,
        "end": 242779,
        "text": "And today I'm driving the release cut. Plan's still Thursday afternoon, so four o'clock today. If you've got something that needs to be in, merge it by three thirty."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 243220,
        "end": 246160,
        "text": "And the quarantined test won't block the cut?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 246727,
        "end": 252482,
        "text": "No, quarantined tests still run but they don't gate anything. No blockers from me."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 253183,
        "end": 255618,
        "text": "Great, thanks. Tom, you're up."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 256347,
        "end": 265577,
        "text": "Hey. So, queue-wise it's a lot calmer. We closed fourteen tickets yesterday, and nine of them were Fernhollow cleanup confirmations."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 265862,
        "end": 275307,
        "text": "Owen replied this morning. He's on the release notes list now, his two dispatch leads too, and he asked when the postmortem is landing."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 275593,
        "end": 284438,
        "text": "He also said his dispatchers have stopped double-checking every recurring job by hand, which, I think, is the real sign it's over."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 285024,
        "end": 291414,
        "text": "Still Friday. I'm finishing it tonight and I'll send it to Owen tomorrow, with you on copy."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 291934,
        "end": 303034,
        "text": "Perfect. The other thing, there's a new ticket from one of the smaller plumbing accounts. One technician's jobs are showing an hour off in his Outlook calendar."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 303308,
        "end": 312483,
        "text": "He's in a different time zone from his dispatcher, and I don't know yet if it's us or Microsoft. It's only the one technician so far."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 312845,
        "end": 322700,
        "text": "Hmm, that sounds like the time zone on the series master, we've seen something like that before with recurring events. It might be the, um..."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 323534,
        "end": 329644,
        "text": "Let's take that one offline. Maya, Tom, can you grab ten minutes straight after this?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 330258,
        "end": 331633,
        "text": "Yep, works for me."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 332189,
        "end": 337574,
        "text": "Sure, I'll send a huddle link right after. That's it from me, no blockers."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 337879,
        "end": 348369,
        "text": "Oh, and Noor and I might have the onboarding survey results by next week, depending on how many come back. She's out today, so I'm just flagging it."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 349230,
        "end": 358025,
        "text": "Me, quickly. Yesterday was one on ones and hiring. We've got two more senior backend screens on the calendar for next week."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 358197,
        "end": 365567,
        "text": "Today I'm on the Fernhollow postmortem, and I'll review Maya's renewal design once it's ready, no rush on that."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 365961,
        "end": 376511,
        "text": "And a reminder for everyone, Maya's off the on-call rotation for the next two weeks. I'm primary for anything sync related and Diego's secondary this weekend."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 377158,
        "end": 382398,
        "text": "Yep, I've read the runbook twice. Please nobody break anything on Saturday."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 383265,
        "end": 390955,
        "text": "Oh, and someone floated moving standup to async on Fridays. I'm not deciding that today, just think about it."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 391841,
        "end": 394521,
        "text": "I'd vote for that, for what it's worth."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 394896,
        "end": 398101,
        "text": "I'm neutral. As long as people actually post."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 398962,
        "end": 412037,
        "text": "Noted. Okay, recap. Maya adds the field by end of day tomorrow, Priya quarantines the test and cuts at four, merge by three thirty, and Maya and Tom take the Outlook thing offline."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Shreyas",
        "isMe": true,
        "start": 412452,
        "end": 414827,
        "text": "Thanks, all. Have a good one."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 415573,
        "end": 417513,
        "text": "Thanks, everyone, bye now."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 417934,
        "end": 423229,
        "text": "Wait, quick one, did the office coffee machine die again or is it just me?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 424085,
        "end": 429290,
        "text": "It's not dead, someone unplugged it for the vacuum. I'll plug it back in."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Diego Alvarez",
        "isMe": false,
        "start": 429890,
        "end": 431320,
        "text": "Later, see you all."
      }
    ]
  }
}
